{"lyrics":"[00:00.22]What do you see in Juice WRLD?\n[00:01.28]Like, talk about the talent that you see from him\n[00:03.12]You just brought him out on stage in front of all these people\n[00:05.28]I see you said he is like the best freestyler alive\n[00:07.14]He like\n[00:08.80]He like that 2009 or 2000\n[00:09.78]He probably like the 2006, maybe 2006 to 2009 Lil Wayne\n[00:12.72]He that, he that nigga\n[00:13.46]And then they sit here do the, uh\n[00:15.32]He'll do another version of the song or freestyle (Yup?)\n[00:19.40]He did like three, three, four songs\n[00:20.26]Over one beat\n[00:21.02]All freestyle, like which one we like\n[00:22.32]Yeah, man, just let me know, I'ma text you\n[00:23.46]Aight, bet\n[00:23.70]For sure guys\n[00:24.16]For sure bro\n[00:25.10]I fuck with you bro\n[00:25.60]Nice to meet y'all bro\n[00:26.30]Aight bro, aight bro\n[00:26.74]Be blessed, bro (Yes)\n[00:29.38]Yeah, you too, bro\n[00:39.38]Congratulations on your...\n[00:44.20]Yo, shoutout to Juice too, man\n[00:45.74]Like, yo, he, that kid was so talented, man\n[00:48.72]He like, his, his freestyle he did on Westwood (Brr)\n[00:51.04]Where he rapped for an hour, like what the fuck?\n[00:54.12]And to be so young\n[00:56.24]He like mastered that so fucking quickly (Yeah)\n[00:59.66]It's really sad man, that, that\n[01:01.94]Like his potential was so off the charts\n[01:04.32]Period\n[01:04.72]You know who the best freestyler I've ever seen is? (Yeah?)\n[01:06.90]Juice WRLD\n[01:07.56]Juice, yeah\n[01:08.16]Have you ever seen his freestyles? (Yeah)\n[01:09.58]They're, they're so, they're never-ending\n[01:11.90]He can do it for like an hour\n[01:12.86]And and he makes total sense the entire time\n[01:15.76]And is actually really, like good, like intricate flow patterns\n[01:18.78]He, like to me, he was the best freestyler I've ever seen\n[01:21.30]And he was like the best hitmak- he was like\n[01:23.90]I really feel like he was the most\n[01:24.96]Talented, eh, like songwriter in music\n[01:27.70]If, I can't imagine there just goin' in there and doin' one-\n[01:30.10]Juice did that, my friend, Benny worked with Juice (Yeah?)\n[01:32.58]And would say, he would go in the booth\n[01:34.30]Go three minutes over the beat, and it be a hit\n[01:36.82]And then he said, \"Okay, another one\"\n[01:38.20]And then he'd go three minutes over the beat\n[01:39.58]And it be a different hit (Shit)\n[01:41.24]And then he'd be like, \"Just pick whatever version you want\"\n[01:43.24]He would tell Benny to cut it up?\n[01:44.42]No, not even cut it up, just like pick\n[01:45.84]What hit do you want?\n[01:46.88]He freestyled- the whole song is freestyled (Ugh)\n[01:49.44]Hits (Ugh)\n[01:50.60]Like smash hits\n[01:51.88]How, how, how?\n[01:52.78]I sit in my room for six months and write a verse\n[01:55.84]This guy goes in there and it's four minutes and it's a smash\n[01:58.84]I think, like, what\n[02:00.62]What Juice was to our generation, bro\n[02:04.22]And the impact he had on us is what Biggie did for New York, for real\n[02:08.20]Like, I really think, um, what, he had that, like that Biggie, Pac effect\n[02:13.38]You know what I'm sayin'?\n[02:14.56]In his short time here","words":[[0.22,0.28,"What"],[0.32,0.34,"do"],[0.38,0.42,"you"],[0.5,0.62,"see"],[0.66,0.7,"in"],[0.76,1.02,"Juice"],[1.06,1.14,"WRLD?"],[1.28,1.4,"Like,"],[1.46,1.62,"talk"],[1.68,1.88,"about"],[2.06,2.12,"the"],[2.16,2.38,"talent"],[2.46,2.52,"that"],[2.58,2.62,"you"],[2.68,2.74,"see"],[2.84,2.94,"from"],[2.98,3.02,"him"],[3.12,3.18,"You"],[3.22,3.34,"just"],[3.38,3.52,"brought"],[3.56,3.6,"him"],[3.64,3.72,"out"],[3.78,3.82,"on"],[3.9,4.06,"stage"],[4.12,4.14,"in"],[4.18,4.3,"front"],[4.36,4.38,"of"],[4.42,4.5,"all"],[4.62,4.7,"these"],[4.76,4.9,"people"],[5.28,5.28,"I"],[5.38,5.5,"see"],[5.54,5.6,"you"],[5.68,5.86,"said"],[5.9,5.92,"he"],[6.0,6.1,"is"],[6.14,6.26,"like"],[6.3,6.34,"the"],[6.4,6.6,"best"],[6.64,6.96,"freestyler"],[7.02,7.1,"alive"],[7.14,7.16,"He"],[7.26,7.44,"like"],[8.8,8.